From 713c3ae9db374d9882922037afc8a89bb1ce2cd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Merlin Kooshmanian <mkooshmanian@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Mar 2026 16:42:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] sched/tgbs: add optional root task-group bandwidth
 server

Add an optional TG bandwidth server for the root task group.

When enabled, root-cgroup tasks run on a per-CPU virtual rq served
by a root CBS, while idle and stop tasks remain on the physical rq.

Derive the root runtime from the residual DEADLINE bandwidth left
after its direct children and keep it aligned with the root active
server mask.

Recompute the root reservation when a direct child changes runtime or
period, when a child is onlined or released, when the effective
cpuset changes, or when the global DEADLINE bandwidth is updated.

Also account root TG servers in rd->dl_bw.total_bw so they coexist
properly with the fair server on the physical rq.

With CONFIG_ROOT_TG_BANDWIDTH_SERVER disabled, behavior is unchanged.
